        <headline>Flood Warning issued September 25 at 5:40AM EDT until September 25 at 12:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston WV</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...Central Gallia County in southeastern Ohio...
Southeastern Vinton County in southeastern Ohio...

* WHEN...Until noon EDT Friday.

* IMPACTS...Flooding of Raccoon Creek and it's tributaries is
occurring. Numerous roads remain closed due to flooding. Low-water
crossings are inundated with water and may not be passable.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 537 AM EDT, Flooding of Raccoon Creek and it's tributaries
continues, with numerous roadways flooded. Water levels are
dropping however. Motorists should continue to exercise extreme
caution and be prepared for water or debris remaining on
roadways. Please continue to heed remaining road closures.

- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Rio Grande, Vinton, Wilkesville, Adamsville and Radcliffe.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Stay away or be swept away. River banks and culverts can become
unstable and unsafe.</instruction>
